  "note": "The four Hebrew verb keys p.cu.aa/ac, p.cv.ac and p.cw.aa duplicate the same tokens. Count one set; even it includes two child nouns. The child key also includes a gleaning verb in Jer 6:9. Omitted xp.ag.aa from the Aramaic verb because it would count thousands of prepositions, which belong to alah. The SEDRA enter family is root 1378, lexemes 2313–2318; the infant is lexeme 2269. The Punic form directly parallels the shorter infant noun; its bearing on the expanded Hebrew form is semantic as well as formal. The Arabic collar is a possible parallel for the yoke. Links from deeds to the child, yoke and refining vessel remain uncertain. No clear personal name appears among the keys. The suggested Geʿez infant parallel remains to be checked against its dictionary."
